cards.en:
Because only the top of a stack can be accessed, many algorithms move all items to another stack. Moving every item of A into B <b>reverses the order</b>:<pre>Sub-program reverse(A, B)
  while not isEmpty(A)
    push(B, pop(A))</pre>The top of A becomes the <b>bottom</b> of B, and the bottom of A becomes the <b>top</b> of B. Afterwards A is empty.<br><br>Key facts:<ul><li>Reversing twice (A → B → A) restores the <b>original order</b>.</li><li>This gives access to the <b>bottom</b> item: after reverse(S1, S2), the original bottom of S1 is on top of S2.</li><li>The same idea reverses a string: push each character, then pop all.</li></ul>

cards.zh:
Stack 只能操作顶端，所以很多算法会把全部数据搬到另一个 stack。把 A 全搬到 B 会<b>倒转次序</b>：<pre>Sub-program reverse(A, B)
  while not isEmpty(A)
    push(B, pop(A))</pre>A 的顶变 B 的<b>底</b>，A 的底变 B 的<b>顶</b>，A 变空。<br><br>要点：reverse 两次恢复<b>原次序</b>；可借此取到原来的<b>底部</b>项；同样方法可倒转字符串（逐字 push，再全部 pop）。

